      "id": "GGD-02",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "title": "Rank induction identifies the coordinate fibre measure as an Euler product with constant one",
      "anchor": "lifts-global-gram-ranks",
      "statement": "The normalized global measure has a coordinate-measure Euler factorization with constant 1 in the stated strict-rank range. A represented first line reduces both source and Gram ranks by one. A missing first line gives a zero global measure and a vanishing local factor. Unit-mass errors for standard finite lattices are absolutely summable.",
