    {
      "id": "GGD-03",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "title": "Self-dual normalization preserves the product of local Gram densities",
      "anchor": "lifts-global-gram-normalize",
      "statement": "For self-dual source and target Haar measures, the continuous density at an invertible target is the integral over its reference Gram fibre multiplied by cᵥ/eᵥ. These ratios have product one including infinity. Hence the archimedean density times the convergent product of finite densities equals the normalized rational Gram mean.",
      "hypotheses": "Coordinate fibre measures disintegrate the matrix Haar measure over the Hermitian target measure. The local scalar Fourier characters are components of one global character. The finite test factors are compactly supported and the archimedean factor has Schwartz decay. The self-dual scalings satisfy the product-one law.",
      "equations": [
        "lifts-global-gram-scale"
      ],
