  "outstanding": [
    "In dimension at least three OVM determines the one-vector scalar by comparing the discrepancy at every dilation to the lower bound on a subsequence. BEQ derives equidistribution, the uniform truncation of the scalar Euler product and the volume comparison in the binary case. Rational representation and transport of a common scalar by similitudes remain separate inputs. Local disintegration, Schwartz estimates at infinity and the product normalization of self-dual measures enter the higher-rank argument."
  ]
}
